		<!--
  RBM's own sounds. Audio files go in RBMXML/ModuleSounds/ (copied to RBM/ModuleSounds/ by the RBM post-build step);
  `path` is the file name inside that folder. Format, categories and the playing code: see Native/ModuleData/module_sounds.xml.

  Crowd grunt (FormationShoutsLogic): the only grunt soldiers give - every march beat, the settled halt, the closed
  shield wall/square/circle and the formation's answer to an order. Looked up as rbm/march/<culture> (empire, vlandia,
  sturgia, battania, aserai, khuzait, nord - the leader's culture) or rbm/march/generic for any other culture. No
  fallback between them: a missing entry means silence.

  march_crowd_*.ogg, all cut from "CRWDBatl_Crowd Grunting, Exerting, Metered, Rowing" by ShangusBurger / Shane Vincent,
  GameSoundCon 2024 walla session, CC0 (see ModuleSounds/README.md):
      1-8    the eight grunts, XY-AKG214 take (freesound.org/s/763822)
      9-16   the same eight, spaced-omni take (freesound.org/s/764266) - same performance, wider room
      17-22  two different grunts of 1-8 layered 15-40 ms apart, for a bigger crowd
  One recording set, so the cultures differ by pitch: Sturgians and Nords deeper, Khuzaits and Aserai lighter,
  Battanians loosest.

  Horns (FormationShoutsLogic), single blasts played at the formation's man nearest the camera:
    rbm/horn/charge/<culture>  a mounted formation (cavalry, horse archers) going over to Charge, before its yells;
                               same 7 cultures as the march grunt, else rbm/horn/charge/generic
    rbm/horn/order/<culture>   Aserai and Nord formations, with every order (aserai, nord only, no generic)
  No fallback between entries: a missing entry means no horn.
  Category mission_siege_loud: the 3D category for the loudest battlefield events (big explosions), so a horn carries
  further than the shouts; its 8 s limit covers the longest blast (horn_d_1, 7.6 s). Not alert: that one is pseudo-3D,
  and a horn must still be heard from where it is blown. The code also pulls a far horn closer (Horn* distances).
  All CC0, from Freesound's HQ previews (see ModuleSounds/README.md):
      horn_viking_1-12   "medieval viking horn" by Artiom_Constantinov (freesound.org/s/856540), deep, 2.4-3.4 s
      horn_d_1           "Viking Horn in D" by roemergruft (freesound.org/s/704440), 7.6 s long blast
      horn_d_2           the same blast cut to 4 s with a fade
      horn_battle_1      "Battle_horn_1" by kirmm (freesound.org/s/392180), 4.5 s, with echo
      horn_shofar_1-5    "Small Shofar" by Sauron974 (freesound.org/s/223368), ram's horn, 1.5-5.9 s
      horn_shofar_6      "shofar blast medium length two tone" by Sonicsheep (freesound.org/s/479310), 2.7 s
  Empire and Vlandia blow the brass-like battle horn, Sturgians, Nords and Battanians the viking horn (Sturgians
  deepest), Khuzaits and Aserai the ram's horn (Khuzaits the long, lower blasts).
  -->
